<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111021" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλ-ήτωρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lover</i> (<span class="entity">Cretan</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.4.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as fem., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δὲ . . κεῖται φ. τοῦδε</span> here lies
			his <i>paramour,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1446
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷδε</span> Sch., who derives
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλήτωρ</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦτορ</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγαλήτωρ</span>), the one <i>dear to</i> his
			<i>heart,</i> his <i>darling</i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as Adj., <i>loving,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγοστός, κόλπος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				3.398
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				21.27
			</span></i>.</div>
